Date: Tue, 20 Oct 2026 23:11:10 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Give a game folder's mods to the game's own title only

Eden asks for the mods of every title it patches, the game's DLC and update among them. A game
folder's mods (roms/<Game>/mods) were given for all of them, while the mods switched off in the
launcher are on the game's own title's disabled list. A mod switched off for the game still
applied to its DLC's data: Mario Kart 8 Deluxe with its Booster Course DLC and a mod in its
game folder did not start, switched off or not (issue 281). The game folder's mods and cheats
now go to the game's own title alone, as mods/<title ID>/ always did.

tools/check-game-folder-mods.py (in the release build's source checks) compiles mods.h, makes
a game folder with a mod and a cheat file, and checks that the game's title gets them and its
DLC, its update and other titles do not.
